{"chunk_id": "538801a82bf0", "text": "In a ferocious clash between the Gods and the Rakshasas, the battlefield becomes a gruesome spectacle where celestial hosts and demons slaughter one another amid rivers of blood. Ravana (Dashagriva), enraged at the destruction of his forces, plunges into the fray and challenges Indra himself. Their duel fills the sky with arrows until darkness shrouds the battle. Indra attempts to contain Ravana, knowing he cannot kill him due to a boon, and instead urges the gods to capture him. Amid the chaos, Ravana\u2019s son Ravani (Meghanada), using magical invisibility and supernatural power, strikes at the exhausted Indra, binds him through sorcery, and carries him away captive. With the king of the gods seized, Ravani urges Ravana to withdraw, declaring victory and humiliating the celestial hosts\u2014an episode that foreshadows his later fame as Indrajit, the conqueror of Indra.\nDuring a chaotic battle between gods and Rakshasas, Ravana\u2019s son Meghnada uses magic to defeat and capture Indra, forcing the gods into retreat.\nThemes: divine warfare, Ravana's ambition, Meghnada's prowess, illusion and magic in battle, capture of Indra", "vector": [0.006805623881518841, -0.021015498787164688, 0.005959519185125828, 0.021283041685819626, -0.0041970801539719105, 0.018888533115386963, -0.032105155289173126, -0.03427225351333618, -0.031249016523361206, -0.017978886142373085, 0.012594584375619888, 0.013370458967983723, 0.022112425416707993, -0.007645039819180965, -0.0021052286028862, 0.01020007487386465, 0.03306831046938896, -0.022527117282152176, 0.030018320307135582, -0.011424084194004536, 0.0011939104879274964, -0.0007349070510827005, -0.014888765290379524, 0.018366822972893715, -0.03293453902006149, 0.009036263450980186, 0.010588012635707855, -0.0315433144569397, 0.0294297244399786, -0.012507633306086063, -0.007645039819180965, -0.024667460471391678, 0.004484688863158226, -0.014380433596670628, -0.015477360226213932, -0.00669191824272275